# Edits of the book's commands: <section id><TAB><sed -E expression>.
# An expression that changes nothing stops the build (the book changed).
#
# YVIS is installed on other machines than the one that builds it. The book
# (8.2.3, 8.23, 8.51) requires generic builds of GMP and Libffi in that
# case: by default both are optimised for the build machine's CPU and
# crash with "Illegal instruction" elsewhere. x86-64 is the baseline every
# 64-bit PC implements.
ch-system-gmp	s|--docdir=/usr/share/doc/gmp-[0-9.]+|& --host=none-linux-gnu|
ch-system-libffi	s|--with-gcc-arch=native|--with-gcc-arch=x86-64|
#
# 8.84 Stripping: "A large number of files will be flagged as errors because
# their file format is not recognized. These warnings can be safely ignored.
# They indicate that those files are scripts, not binaries." Sections run
# with `bash -e`, so the errors of that last loop (and only that one) are
# tolerated explicitly.
ch-system-stripping	s/(\* \) strip --strip-unneeded \$i)$/\1 || true/
